id: goof
name: Goof
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
special: true
usageLimit: 1/round
exploitable: All adjacent Opponents.
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Clash (Morale) at an Opponent not at Long Range - won, a 1d4: Impaired, Prone, Impediment or Sleeping till the start of your next turn.
text: >
  Goof Maneuver [1/Round]: With a whimsical gag out of seemingly nowhere, you expose your foe’s vulnerabilities.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: N/A
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: All adjacent Opponents.
  –Effect: Target an Opponent who is not at Long Range. Make a Clash (Morale) against them. If you win, roll a 1d4. That Opponent gains the Combat Condition rolled until the start of your next turn:
  * 1) Impaired.
  * 2) Prone.
  * 3) Impediment.
  * 4) Sleeping.

---

# A Special Maneuver: open where an effect grants it - the Gadabout Vocation. Used, which Opponent asked, and the Clash
# opened; won, the 1d4 rolled on its card and its Combat Condition put on them, on your clock (chat.mjs goof, settleGoof).
[on used]
goof();
